      "title": "The cheaper policy",
      "narration": "Rosa receives a mailer offering a disability income policy for thirty dollars less a month than the one Theo sold her two years ago. Replacement means dropping or reducing existing coverage to buy new coverage. It is lawful and sometimes wise, but it resets clocks. A new disability or long-term care policy brings a new pre-existing condition look-back, a new probationary period and a new contestable period. Rosa’s back condition, now covered after two years, could become a pre-existing condition under the new policy. The first replacement question is always: what coverage has the client already earned?",
